<title>USA: Terra Nova to buy back up to $20 mln of shrs.</title>
<headline>Terra Nova to buy back up to $20 mln of shrs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Terra Nova (Bermuda) Holdings Ltd said Monday it plans to buy back up to $20 million of its common stock.</p>
<p>The repurchases are to be made from time to time on the open market at prevailing market prices or in privately negotiated transactions, it said.</p>
<p>In afternoon trading on Monday, Terra Nova's shares were trading at about 19-3/8.</p>
<p>The company said that any shares repurchased would be held in trust and would be available for the exercise of outstanding employee stock options and director share units, or for other corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
